From: Dmitry Grinberg <dmitryg@ceragon.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Apr 2025 17:40:42 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Siklu dropbear source changes

Resolve users through _getpwnam()/_getpwuid() from siklu_pwd.h instead
of getpwnam()/getpwuid(), authenticate through PAM instead of the
password file, export the PAM environment into the process environment
and keep it by not calling clearenv(), so the CLI gets what the remote
AAA server returned, lower MAX_UNAUTH_CLIENTS from 30 to 10 and
MAX_CHANNELS from 1000 to 10, and log PAM authentication and account
failures at LOG_NOTICE instead of LOG_WARNING.

Keep the session process root after authentication
(DROPBEAR_SVR_DROP_PRIVS 0), as dropbear 2024.86 did: with privilege
dropping the session writes utmp, wtmp and lastlog through a utmp group,
which the rootfs does not have, so a remote AAA user's (uid 900)
successful login would miss wtmp, where the configuration daemon reads
it. Stream (unix socket) forwarding requires privilege dropping, so it
is off.

[Dima Weber: re-derived for dropbear 2026.94; DROP_PRIVS and stream
forwarding off]
Upstream: N/A, Siklu-specific change
Signed-off-by: Dima Weber <diepress@gmail.com>
